 "title": "A law with no coins has a round circle",
 "subject": "Whether a deterministic logical law, with no chance, can have a round circle of bond distance",
 "conclusion": "On Conway and Radin's pinwheel tiling, the parity laws with knots at tile corners or on tiles have bond distances, counts of distinctions with no lengths, that grow at the same rate in every direction: exactly round circles with no chance involved. The proof is an isotropy principle: a rotation-invariant tiling space uniquely ergodic under translations makes every covariant bond distance round.",
